    "summary": "On 2026-11-12 at 14:20, haul truck HT-07 caught fire on the Pit 3 ramp at a fictional mine. A hydraulic hose had ruptured at 14:05 and sprayed oil onto a hot turbo surface. The turbo heat shield was not in place after a rebuild. The cab log shows the truck still moving after the hydraulic alarm started at 14:10. On-board suppression was activated at 14:19, but the nozzle facing the turbo was blocked by a shipping cap. The ramp was closed until 20:20. One fact is still open: the rebuild pack list has not been found, so it is not yet known whether the shield was in the kit. Air at the turbo face is a natural condition and is marked STOP as a desired condition. Selected actions are already in the solution matrix: clamps on the hose run, a heat-shield sign-off, an oil-deflection shield, and a nozzle-cap check on the fire-system PM.",
